  "title": "Low-input nanopore performance \u2014 this study vs prior work",
  "caption": "Low-input nanopore sequencing performance expressed per femtogram of DNA entering library preparation. Each prior-study point is one sample (24 samples from B. Raghavendra et al. 2023, Mojarro et al. 2019, Zorzano et al. 2025); reads/fg = reads/(pg DNA x 1000) and bases/fg = bases/(pg DNA x 1000). This study is shown as Round 1 (n=3) and Round 2 (n=3). Dashed contours are iso-improvement circles around the Round 1 mean (0.1427 reads/fg, 395 bases/fg) at 10x, 100x and 1000x geometric-mean fold improvement in log10-log10 space. Callouts give the largest per-study improvement: B. Raghavendra et al. 2023 (10 pg of E. coli\u2009+\u20092 pg of S. cerevisiae): 714\u00d7 reads, 3,575\u00d7 bases; Mojarro et al. 2019 (2 pg Bacillus spizizenii DNA): 57\u00d7 reads, 150\u00d7 bases; Zorzano et al. 2025 (Microbialite (2800 a)): 1,375\u00d7 reads, 1,828\u00d7 bases. Zorzano et al. 2025 counts use the 'kraken2_q1' variant and Basapathi Raghavendra et al. 2023 the 'kraken2_q10' variant; see prior_studies.tsv for the per-row provenance of every point.",
